# graphify knowledge graph.
#
# This reverses 8bd033bb, which ignored graph.json on the grounds that it is
# ~14MB rewritten whole per rebuild. Two corrections. The size is a raw-bytes
# figure: git zlib-compresses the blob, and the measured cost is 0.9MB per
# revision, not 14MB. And "a fresh clone rebuilds free" only holds for the AST
# and the cached doc extraction — community labelling is a separate LLM pass
# (680 communities here), and dropping .graphify_labels.json means paying it
# again on every clone. Tracking both is cheaper than re-deriving them.
# Tracked (so a clone updates the graph instead of re-extracting it from scratch):
#   graph.json, manifest.json, GRAPH_REPORT.md, cost.json,
#   .graphify_labels.json, cache/semantic/  <- the LLM-extracted part, the only
#   expensive artifact. Content-hash keyed, so it is portable across clones.
# Everything below is machine-local, derived, or a temp from a build in flight.
graphify-out/.graphify_python
graphify-out/.graphify_root
graphify-out/.graphify_chunk_*.json
graphify-out/.graphify_detect.json
graphify-out/.graphify_extract.json
graphify-out/.graphify_ast.json
graphify-out/.graphify_semantic.json
graphify-out/.graphify_semantic_new.json
graphify-out/.graphify_cached.json
graphify-out/.graphify_uncached.txt
graphify-out/.graphify_analysis.json
graphify-out/.needs_update
# stat-index keys on local size+mtime, so it is pure churn in a shared repo.
graphify-out/cache/stat-index.json
graphify-out/cache/last_query_stamp
# AST cache regenerates with no LLM cost and is namespaced per graphify
# version, so committing it churns the whole tree on every upgrade.
graphify-out/cache/ast/
# Derived viz — regenerate with `graphify export html`.
graphify-out/graph.html
# Superseded by the repo-root graphify-out/ (scan root moved apps/ -> repo root).
apps/graphify-out/
# Rollback copy of the cache entries keyed to the old apps/ scan root.
graphify-out/cache/semantic/.pre-rekey-backup/
